"""5J multi-zone building builder (WP1, D2-8). Spain only. Runs on Speed (and anywhere python runs).

`build_mz(row, k, placement, infiltration_ach, north_axis_deg, collapse=False) -> (idf_text, meta)`

Design: Step2_docs/impl/2026-09-30_d2-8_multizone_design.md (items 1-9).
  * `derive(row)` of 4J `4thJ_step8_idf.py` is imported, never copy-edited (plate W x D, height, U-values,
    glazing, capacity c_m x A_C_Ref).
  * n_Storey floors, each h_room high. Roof on the top floor only, ground on the ground floor only.
  * MFH/AB: k dwellings side by side along the long E-W axis on every floor, one zone per dwelling per floor.
    SFH/TH: k = 1, ONE dwelling spanning every floor, one zone per floor.
  * Interzone surfaces (floor/ceiling between storeys, party walls) come in pairs: same area, vertex order
    reversed, each naming the other as Outside Boundary Condition Object. Interior constructions are written
    for BOTH sides (reverse layer order).
  * `collapse=True`: one zone, full height, k = 1 (the old box), for the carry-over gate.

`placement` maps dwelling index j (0..n_dwellings-1, numbered floor by floor, west to east; SFH/TH: only 0) to a
household dict as in 5thJ_idf.py: hid, n_members, presence_csv, appliance_csv, appliance_peak_w.

Every build step prints one `PATCH mz_<name> OK ...` line (and returns the lines in meta["patch_lines"]).
"""
